# A UNC path (starting with `\`) gets the path help.
mode: syntax
---- query
from '\\server\share\x.csv' | take 1
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..37
  PIPELINE@0..36
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..27
      STRING@5..27 "'\\\\server\\share\\x.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@27..28 " "
    PIPE@28..29 "|"
    WHITESPACE@29..30 " "
    TAKE_OP@30..36
      IDENT@30..34 "take"
      WHITESPACE@34..35 " "
      LITERAL@35..36
        LONG@35..36 "1"
  WHITESPACE@36..37 "\n"

error[DS0005]: unknown escape sequence `\s`
  --> query:1:15
  |
1 | from '\\server\share\x.csv' | take 1
  |               ^^    -- `\x` is not valid either
  |               |
  |               not a valid escape
  |
  = help: if this is a Windows path, use a verbatim string `@'\\server\share\x.csv'` or forward slashes `'//server/share/x.csv'`
  = note: valid escapes are `\\`, `\"`, `\'`, `\n`, `\r`, `\t`, `\0` and `\u{...}`
